/*
================================================================================
📌 MainScope — THEORY
================================================================================

1️⃣ What is MainScope?
---------------------
MainScope() is a READY-MADE CoroutineScope provided by Kotlin.

Internally (simplified), it is defined as:

MainScope() = CoroutineScope(
    Dispatchers.Main + SupervisorJob()
)

So it already contains:
✔ Dispatcher → Dispatchers.Main (UI thread)
✔ Job        → SupervisorJob (lifecycle & cancellation)

That is why we DO NOT manually pass Dispatcher or Job.


2️⃣ When to use MainScope?
-------------------------
- UI-related coroutine work
- Helper / Logic / Presenter classes
- When lifecycleScope or viewModelScope is NOT available


3️⃣ Is MainScope lifecycle-aware?
--------------------------------
❌ NO

- Android does NOT cancel it automatically
- YOU must cancel it manually
- Forgetting to cancel → MEMORY LEAK


4️⃣ What happens when MainScope is cancelled?
---------------------------------------------
- All coroutines inside it are cancelled
- The scope becomes DEAD
- A cancelled scope CANNOT be reused
- To run again → create a NEW MainScope()


5️⃣ MainScope vs Custom CoroutineScope
-------------------------------------
Custom Scope:
CoroutineScope(Dispatchers.Main + Job())
→ You provide everything manually

MainScope:
MainScope()
→ Kotlin provides Dispatcher + Job internally


================================================================================
📌 GOLDEN RULE
================================================================================

✔ MainScope is simple but dangerous if misused
✔ Always cancel it when work is finished
✔ Cancelled scope must be recreated to reuse
*/
